   procedure="Before day one the hiring manager confirms the workspace, requests accounts, and assigns an onboarding buddy, and equipment is ordered through IT Asset Management. On the first day the new hire completes identity verification, enrolls MFA, and signs required policies, and orientation covers security awareness and payroll. Role-specific access is requested through the internal system and approved by resource owners following least privilege.",
   required="Onboarding requires the confirmed hire record, the role profile, the start date, and the list of systems the new hire needs. The new hire must complete identity verification and policy acknowledgements, and managers track outstanding items on the checklist until all are closed.",
   approval="Resource owners approve role-specific access requests, and managers confirm completion of mandatory training before probation ends. Account creation itself follows the new account provisioning manual, which requires a verified hire record before any credentials are issued.",
   exceptions="Same-day or remote starts may use an expedited setup with manager attestation and prompt follow-up verification. Any access request that cannot be tied to a confirmed hire, or that exceeds the role profile, is paused and escalated to the manager and identity team.",
   records="Onboarding completion, policy acknowledgements, and access approvals are retained according to operating standards for audit and to support later access reviews. Probation check-in outcomes are recorded, and records are kept per retention requirements.",
