   required="An expense claim should include itemized receipts, the business purpose of each expense, the date, the amount, and the cost center. Expenses must be reasonable, necessary, and supported by valid documentation, and claims missing receipts or justification are returned for correction.",
   approval="The line manager approves claims within their threshold, and amounts above it require additional approval before payment. Results are communicated within one to two business days of approval, and payment follows in the next scheduled cycle to the registered account.",
   exceptions="Where a receipt is genuinely unavailable, a documented declaration may be accepted at the approver's discretion for small amounts. Duplicate or inflated claims are rejected and, where intent is suspected, escalated to finance and Human Resources for review.",
   records="Claims, receipts, approvals, and payment records are retained according to operating standards for audit and tax purposes. Cost-center allocations are reconciled, and records are kept in line with finance retention requirements before disposal.",
